    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on darwin1859-ch10-13: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.68";
    dc:description "The relationship is measurable for many well-sampled clades, but no harmonized dataset spans the stated scope. Phylogenetic structure also makes a simple age-distance trend only moderately discriminating.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Within clades having morphological matrices, calculate distance from each fossil to extant relatives and regress it on fossil age while controlling for phylogeny and missing characters. A generally positive age-distance relation supports the claim.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Distance depends on character selection and extant survivor bias.", "Morphological matrices are curated for selected clades rather than all life.";
